==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*toores}}, of {{etyl|bat|fi}} origin (compare Lithuanian {{m|lt|dõras||good}}), with the suffix {{m|fi|-e}}. The same reshaping has been applied in Karelian {{m|krl|tuoreh}} and Votic {{m|vot|toorõh}}. Estonian {{m|et|toores}} retains the original stem type.

[[Category:Finnish words suffixed with -e]]

